what's about the new documentary obvi  this is a true story about the horrific  events that occurred in Paris Paris  November 2015 and and for those of you  just just take people back to the events  yeah and what it is you wanted to sort  of accomplish with yeah so on that  evening there were a series of sort of  coordinated attacks across Paris at  various different locations and and the  one that was the the most discussed  almost that definitely had the most loss  of life was a concert that was held at a  place called Tabata claun and the band  the Eagles of Death Metal were playing  at that venue in 89 people lost their  lives and it was you know along with all  of the other events that night was  really really sad and tragic and I am  very good friends with with the guys in  the band and they had actually been  doing a bunch of stuff with me for the  tower documentary when we were finishing  that up and then November happened and a  few months afterwards luckily you know  the band was able to make it out of  there but they went back to Paris last  February to finish their concert to  finish their show and we sort of decided  kind of last minute  that maybe it would be a good thing to  go and sort of document them going back  and not really for any other reason than  then to show the the band and their fans  collectively coming together and trying  to make something positive out of a  really horrible situation the it's  interesting because it the documentary  as they often do you start out with  maybe one in ten or even not knowing  what your intent is and then that can  change when a filmmaker makes a  conventional film they know what their  story is a documentary filmmaker has to  find the story as they're going what was  the story you found you obviously that  was your intention but what did you find  well we yeah we we knew that was gonna  we knew we were gonna focus on the  return concert we knew we were obviously  going to talk about the the events of  the bodycon but we didn't really know  what how to start the film off and  knowing jesse hughes the lead singer  in Joshua Homme you or the two founding  members knowing them as well as I do I  sort of instinctually knew about their  relationship they've got one of the best  relationships I've ever seen I mean they  really are in fact there was someone who  saw the movie last week and they said  that they feel they've watched the first  love story of 2017 by seeing these two  guys because they really have a genuine  deep bond for each other and have always  been there for each other and it really  started normally when I started  interviewing someone for a talk I'll  I'll ask them questions just to get them  comfortable on camera and get them  talking so I would just ask them like  how'd you two meet and there they are  two sharp-witted very funny very  likeable guys that have a deep bond and  about halfway through that first  interview my producing partner who is my  best friend who I grew up with he came  up to me says oh I see what you're doing  here these are like the two main  characters that we're gonna follow and  it ended up being a happy accident and  it ended up being a great way to set her  set up the film because you know Jessie  and Josh are so close but Joshua doesn't  really tour with the group right so he  wasn't there the night of the attacks  and so you have these two best friends  that are literally an ocean apart on the  worst night of their lives and and it's  about how one was able to be there for  you know for the other and vice versa  during this really difficult time it's  it's a really sweet a loving film that  I'm very proud of and I'm just really  honored that my friends were able to to  let me help them in any way I could  you
 

